            "qNo": 2,
            "unit": 1,
            "question": "State the difference between Singly Linked List and Doubly Linked List.",
            "answer": "A Singly Linked List has nodes containing one pointer pointing to the next node, allowing only unidirectional traversal. A Doubly Linked List contains two pointers (next and previous) per node, enabling bidirectional traversal and O(1) deletion of a given node.",
